From 378b738a8a8e1a2735456ca0baee22d564e10193 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 10:01:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 132/217] fix(perf): enforce protocol outlier gate and per-side
 warmup in G2 verdict

D1: _variance_verdict now implements protocol step 6
(outlier_ratio > 0.10 -> UNSTABLE) before the cv/p95 ceilings, and
aggregate recomputes each round-case verdict from raw statistics instead of
trusting the stored verdict.

D9: a case stability verdict now requires cuBLAS warmup PASS as well as
pypto_x warmup PASS (stability.reasons lists each failed component).

D2: a key enters the ratio gate only when kernel-dominated in every selected
round (dispatch_dominated_any false); per-round shares/domination are stored.

D8: G2 is enforced on gate-relevant (kernel-dominated) keys and both the
scope and the excluded dispatch-dominated keys/verdicts are reported.

Aggregate also voids a whole round when any kernel-dominated case in that
round fails G2, so gate.relative cannot be G3_ELIGIBLE on a partially invalid
round set. No thresholds are frozen.
